	(text "PERIPHERAL BUS -- eight 2x25 0.1in card-edge slots on the core PCB.\nPin table: .git/sdd/PERIPHERAL_BUS.md section 1. Generated by docs/notes/bus_gen.py\nfrom one table; the symbol, the footprints and the card projects come from the same table.\nSlot decode stays ON THE CARD ('138 on M11-M13, Rico 2026-09-12). Slot n = 0x4000 + n*0x800.\nCLK_B: ~{CLK} through one '04 section; no card's clock pin ever sees U27.5 raw.\n~{IRQ} ~{NMI} ~{DMARQ} ~{DMAAK} RDY: named, RESERVED, not driven. Spares: no-connect.\nRails are what the picoPSU delivers (POWER.md SECTION 8). -12V is 50-100mA for the WHOLE\nmachine: every card states its +/-12V draw on its root page.\nSocket footprint is a PLACEHOLDER pin array until the part is chosen (OPEN 2)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
